commit 0edd3e5214f88e13cb78d0647fb16847bcc32357
Author: Minxi Hou <houminxi@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jul 26 08:29:44 2026 -0400

    risk: persistent state machine prevents drawdown whipsaw
    
    Replace the per-day stateless hard breaker with an explicit state
    machine (NORMAL/SOFT_REDUCED/BUY_HALT/LIQUIDATED) that prevents
    liquidate->rebuy->liquidate oscillation through a lockdown mechanism.
    
    The state machine is shadow-first (default shadow, zero behavior
    change).  In shadow mode it logs transitions to risk_shadow_log but
    the existing risk.py logic keeps full authority.  Enforce mode
    requires a separate order after the G2 gate.
    
    Key changes:
    - New risk_state.py module: state enum, transition logic, persistence,
      migration from is_soft_reduced, shadow logging
    - risk.py: state machine integrated into run_all_risk_checks; daily
      overlays (daily_loss, regime, staleness) remain per-day flags
    - pipeline.py: loads/persists risk_state, handles first-run migration
    - report.py: reads risk_state from paper_state instead of recomputing
      drawdown logic; displays risk state in report
    - ledger.py: adds risk_shadow_log table
    - baseline.yaml: adds state_machine, halt_buys, lockdown_days,
      reentry_dd config keys
    
    Tests: 32 new (state transitions, persistence, migration, shadow
    logging, bug-injection, edge cases) + 46 existing all pass.
    
    Signed-off-by: Minxi Hou <houminxi@gmail.com>

